# MANDATORY: TRANSOVO Date, Time, Timezone & Locale Standards (Guide #10)

**Scope:** All repository work — pages, APIs, `src/lib/`, jobs, and any customer-facing behavior. Read the full source doc before implementing.

**Source of truth:** `docs/TRANSOVO-DATE-TIME-TIMEZONE-LOCALE-STANDARDS.md`

## Hard requirement

Any display, input, storage, or API field involving dates, times, schedules, or timezones **MUST** follow this guide — in UI **and** in `src/lib/` persistence and jobs.

## Non-negotiables

### UI + API + database
- Store/transmit **canonical instant + timezone** — don't lose timezone at boundaries.
- Display in **user/workspace timezone** with explicit timezone when ambiguous.
- **12h vs 24h** follows locale/workspace settings — not hardcoded US-only.
- Relative times ("2 hours ago") include absolute on hover/detail where guide requires.
- Date pickers respect **locale week start** and format.
- Scheduling UI shows **whose timezone** applies (business vs user).
- No off-by-one day bugs from UTC/local confusion — follow canonical temporal architecture.
- Daylight saving transitions handled per guide.
- Cron/jobs/reminders use workspace timezone — not server local time by default.

## On conflict

i18n guide (Guide #11) complements this for format strings.
